  "id": "Compound::DB01340 - Gene::6564",
  "verbalization": "Cilazapril, a drug known for its antihypertensive properties, is shown to bind to Slc15a2, a protein involved in transport processes across cellular membranes. Slc15a2 participates in multiple transport activities, including proton-dependent peptide transport and proton/oligonucleotide cotransport, which are all mediated by the same protein. These activities are linked to Slc15a1, suggesting a potential functional relationship between Slc15a2 and Slc15a1. The evidence suggests that Cilazapril may influence Slc15a1 through its interaction with Slc15a2, which in turn modulates transport functions critical for cellular homeostasis. The consistent binding of Cilazapril to Slc15a2 and its participation in transport activities that are also participated by Slc15a1 implies a possible regulatory or functional link between the drug and the protein. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Slc15a2 as a bridge between Cilazapril and Slc15a1, supporting a mechanism where the drug may affect transport processes via this intermediate protein.",
